@startuml UpsertUserRole Sequence

title Upsert User Role API Sequence

' Leading SQL apostrophes use &#39; so PlantUML preserves literals; parity compares decoded SQL.

' Visual style
skinparam defaultFontName "Sarabun"
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 10
skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor #475569
    ArrowFontColor #334155
    LifeLineBorderColor #CBD5E1
    LifeLineBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
    ParticipantBorderColor #94A3B8
    ParticipantBackgroundColor #F1F5F9
    ParticipantFontColor #0F172A
    GroupBorderColor #94A3B8
    GroupBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
    GroupFontColor #334155
}

' Do not show participant footers at the bottom of the diagram
hide footbox

actor "User" as user
box "Frontend" #F8FAFC
    participant "Upsert User Role Page" as page
end box
box "Web API" #F8FAFC
    participant "API" as api
    participant "Application" as app
    participant "Domain" as domain
    participant "Infrastructure" as infra
end box
box "Database" #F8FAFC
    database "m_user" as m_user
    database "t_user_access_token" as t_user_access_token
    database "m_role" as m_role
    database "t_user_role" as t_user_role
end box

user -> page: Submit the user, role and assignment status
activate page
    page -> api: POST v1/author/user/role/upsert (JSON, Bearer JWT, UTC timestamp)
    activate api
        api -> app: [**UpsertUserRoleCommandHandler**] Process request
        activate app
            note over app, infra
                Execution order: validate the request (400) -> verify JWT (401) -> begin transaction (READ COMMITTED) ->
                lock the caller and target users -> fresh current credentials (401) -> target user existence (404, E10005)
                -> lock the role -> locked assignment existence (404, E10004, only when id supplied) and unchanged user/role
                (400) -> role and user ACTIVE when the request gives the role (404, E10005) -> permission (403, E10009) ->
                duplicate check (409, E10003) -> guarded write -> last administrator rule on the result (409, E10006) ->
                complete mapping -> COMMIT -> response. Every post-BEGIN rejection rolls back.
                Lock order is users (ascending id) -> the role of the request (`FOR UPDATE`) -> the assignment row of `id`
                (`FOR UPDATE`) -> duplicate/count reads and the write. `userId` and `roleId` are immutable, so the request
                touches the `PLATFORM_ADMIN` assignment exactly when the locked role is named `PLATFORM_ADMIN`; two requests
                that take the last administrator away both lock that role row and cannot both pass. Other assignment writers
                must lock the target user and the role in the same order before creating or reopening an assignment, as
                role/permission/scope writers do; this contract does not certify unmigrated writers.
            end note
            app -> app: Generate requestId; validate JSON object/known unique keys/no query, UTC timestamp, optional non-null UUID id, required non-null UUID userId and roleId
            note over app, infra
                HTTP status of the single upsert: Insert 201 Created, Update 200 Ok, Delete 204 No Content (no response
                body), Archive 200 Ok.
                Validate one JSON object allowing only id/userId/roleId/rowStatus, no repeated/unknown body/query keys, JSON
                content type and mandatory UTC timestamp before SQL. id is optional only by omission and is a non-null UUID
                when supplied. userId and roleId are required non-null UUIDs in every request, including delete and archive.
                rowStatus defaults to ACTIVE only when omitted and otherwise is ACTIVE/INACTIVE/DELETED/LOCKED/ARCHIVED;
                insert-DELETED is 400 E10001. Generate requestId when omitted.
                Insert is 201 S10000 Insert User Role Success, existing delete is 204 with no body/status/data, existing
                archive is 200 S10000 Archive User Role Success, and other existing updates are 200 S10000 Update User Role
                Success. SQLSTATE 23505 from uq_t_user_role_user_id_role_id is the final concurrent duplicate guard and maps
                to 409 E10003 The user already has this role. after full rollback. Other SQL/result/mapping errors roll back
                and return generic 500 without bizCode. Timeout before COMMIT rolls back and returns 408 E90001. No retry is
                promised for an unknown commit result.
            end note
            app -> app: Default status ACTIVE only when omitted; reject invalid/null status and insert-DELETED; userId and roleId remain required on delete/archive
            alt Invalid input/header
                break Reject this request
                    app -> api: HTTP 400 E10001
                    api -> page: Show failure; no successful user role action
                    page -> user: Display failure; keep unsaved input
                end break
            else Check passed
            end
            app -> app: Verify JWT signature/issuer/audience/expiry/UUID sub and structured unique roleIds/name array
            alt Missing/invalid JWT or malformed roles
                break Reject this request
                    app -> api: HTTP 401 E10002 Invalid or expired access token.
                    api -> page: Show failure; no successful user role action
                    page -> user: Display failure; keep unsaved input
                end break
            else Check passed
            end
            app -> app: callerUserId = verified sub; accessTokenHash = SHA-256 exact JWT; createdBy/updatedBy = caller UUID string; userIds = distinct callerUserId and request userId; omitted id = typed SQL NULL
            app -> infra: BEGIN READ COMMITTED
            note over app, infra
                Verify JWT signature/issuer/audience/expiry/UUID sub and structured unique roles before BEGIN. roles must be
                an array including [], each role has UUID roleId/non-empty name and roleIds are unique. Malformed/missing
                roles is generic 401 E10002, never [] or live-grant fallback. callerUserId = verified sub; accessTokenHash =
                SHA-256 exact JWT. createdBy/updatedBy are the caller UUID string and now is fresh server UTC, never request
                audit values or timestamp. The request userId is the target user and is distinct from callerUserId.
                Begin READ COMMITTED and lock the distinct caller and target users in one statement in ascending id order
                (`userIds`). Missing caller is 401 with rollback. Capture fresh server UTC now after the lock and recheck
                JWT exp; require matching hash/caller, ACTIVE token/user and strict expired_at > now.
                Revoked/inactive/expired/mismatched credentials are generic 401 before any role or assignment read.
                Logout/reset share the user-first lock. Grant withdrawal alone does not revoke current old claims; refresh
                resolves latest rights.
            end note
            activate infra
            alt Work completes before commit
                note over app, infra
                    Any SQL/result/mapping step may fail, including after a provisional assignment write.
                    Roll back the whole transaction on failure; no success before a successful COMMIT.
                end note
                app -> infra: QUERY - Lock the users
                infra -> m_user: QUERY - Lock the users
                activate m_user
                    note right of m_user
                        SELECT
                            u.id as user_id,
                            u.row_status
                        FROM authen.m_user u
                        WHERE u.id = ANY ('<sequence.userIds>'::UUID[]) -- the caller and the target user, distinct
                        ORDER BY u.id
                        FOR UPDATE
                    end note
                    m_user -> infra: Return locked caller and target user rows or no row
                deactivate m_user
                infra -> app: Return locked caller and target user rows or no row
                alt Caller user missing
                    break Reject this request
                        app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                        app -> api: HTTP 401 E10002 Invalid or expired access token.
                        api -> page: Show failure; no successful user role action
                        page -> user: Display failure; keep unsaved input
                    end break
                else Check passed
                end
                app -> app: Capture fresh server UTC now after the user lock; recheck JWT exp
                alt JWT expired while waiting for the user lock
                    break Reject this request
                        app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                        app -> api: HTTP 401 E10002 Invalid or expired access token.
                        api -> page: Show failure; no successful user role action
                        page -> user: Display failure; keep unsaved input
                    end break
                else Check passed
                end
                app -> infra: QUERY - Check current credential and user
                infra -> t_user_access_token: QUERY - Check current credential and user
                activate t_user_access_token
                    note right of t_user_access_token
                        SELECT
                            at.id as access_token_id
                        FROM authen.t_user_access_token at
                        JOIN authen.m_user u ON u.id = at.user_id
                        WHERE at.token = '<sequence.accessTokenHash>'
                        AND at.user_id = '<sequence.callerUserId>'
                        AND at.row_status = 'ACTIVE'
                        AND at.expired_at > '<sequence.now>'
                        AND u.row_status = 'ACTIVE'
                    end note
                    t_user_access_token -> infra: Return ACTIVE matching unexpired token/user or no row
                deactivate t_user_access_token
                infra -> app: Return ACTIVE matching unexpired token/user or no row
                alt Current token/user missing/inactive/revoked/expired/mismatched
                    break Reject this request
                        app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                        app -> api: HTTP 401 E10002 Invalid or expired access token.
                        api -> page: Show failure; no successful user role action
                        page -> user: Display failure; keep unsaved input
                    end break
                else Check passed
                end
                app -> app: Find the target user in the locked users (any status)
                alt Target user row missing (also when the request takes the role away)
                    break Reject this request
                        app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                        app -> api: HTTP 404 E10005 User not found.
                        api -> page: Show failure; no successful user role action
                        page -> user: Display failure; keep unsaved input
                    end break
                else Check passed
                end
                app -> infra: QUERY - Lock the role
                infra -> m_role: QUERY - Lock the role
                activate m_role
                    note right of m_role
                        SELECT
                            r.id as role_id,
                            r.name,
                            r.row_status
                        FROM author.m_role r
                        WHERE r.id = '<sequence.roleId>' -- the PLATFORM_ADMIN role exactly when the request touches the PLATFORM_ADMIN assignment
                        FOR UPDATE
                    end note
                    m_role -> infra: Return locked role_id/name/row_status or no row
                deactivate m_role
                infra -> app: Return locked role_id/name/row_status or no row
                app -> app: The request touches the PLATFORM_ADMIN assignment exactly when the locked role is named PLATFORM_ADMIN
                alt id is specified (update, delete or archive)
                    app -> infra: QUERY - Lock existing user role
                    infra -> t_user_role: QUERY - Lock existing user role
                    activate t_user_role
                        note right of t_user_role
                            SELECT
                                ur.id as user_role_id,
                                ur.user_id,
                                ur.role_id,
                                ur.row_status
                            FROM author.t_user_role ur
                            WHERE ur.id = '<sequence.id>'
                            AND ur.row_status <> 'DELETED' -- the id of a DELETED row counts as not found
                            FOR UPDATE
                        end note
                        t_user_role -> infra: Return locked user_role_id/user_id/role_id/row_status or no row
                    deactivate t_user_role
                    infra -> app: Return locked user_role_id/user_id/role_id/row_status or no row
                    alt User role not found or DELETED
                        break Reject this request
                            app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                            app -> api: HTTP 404 E10004 User role not found.
                            api -> page: Show failure; no successful user role action
                            page -> user: Display failure; keep unsaved input
                        end break
                    else Check passed
                    end
                    alt userId or roleId differs from the locked row of id
                        break Reject this request
                            app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                            app -> api: HTTP 400 E10001 User Id and Role Id cannot be changed.
                            api -> page: Show failure; no successful user role action
                            page -> user: Display failure; keep unsaved input
                        end break
                    else Check passed
                    end
                else id omitted (insert)
                    app -> app: No assignment row to lock; the users and the role are already locked
                end
                app -> app: Decide whether the request gives the role: an insert, or an update that sets ACTIVE on a locked row that is not ACTIVE
                alt The request gives the role
                    app -> app: Require the locked target user ACTIVE and the locked role present and ACTIVE
                    alt The user or the role is not found or not ACTIVE
                        break Reject this request
                            app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                            app -> api: HTTP 404 E10005 User or role not found or not ACTIVE.
                            api -> page: Show failure; no successful user role action
                            page -> user: Display failure; keep unsaved input
                        end break
                    else Check passed
                    end
                else The request takes the role away or only keeps it
                    app -> app: User and role status are not required
                end
                app -> app: Authorize once using only exact case-sensitive PLATFORM_ADMIN in verified JWT roles; never reload live grants
                alt No exact PLATFORM_ADMIN role claim
                    break Reject this request
                        app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                        app -> api: HTTP 403 E10009 You do not have permission to assign roles.
                        api -> page: Show failure; no successful user role action
                        page -> user: Display failure; keep unsaved input
                    end break
                else Check passed
                end
                app -> infra: QUERY - Check duplicate user role
                infra -> t_user_role: QUERY - Check duplicate user role
                activate t_user_role
                    note right of t_user_role
                        SELECT
                            ur.id as user_role_id
                        FROM author.t_user_role ur
                        WHERE ur.user_id = '<sequence.userId>'
                        AND ur.role_id = '<sequence.roleId>'
                        AND ur.row_status <> 'DELETED'
                        AND ('<sequence.id>' IS NULL OR ur.id <> '<sequence.id>') -- omitted insert id is typed SQL NULL
                    end note
                    t_user_role -> infra: Return the non-DELETED row of the user and the role excluding the optional current id, or no row
                deactivate t_user_role
                infra -> app: Return the non-DELETED row of the user and the role excluding the optional current id, or no row
                alt The user already has the role in a row that is not DELETED
                    break Reject this request
                        app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                        app -> api: HTTP 409 E10003 The user already has this role.
                        api -> page: Show failure; no successful user role action
                        page -> user: Display failure; keep unsaved input
                    end break
                else Check passed
                end
                alt id is omitted (INSERT)
                    app -> infra: INSERT - Create user role
                    infra -> t_user_role: INSERT - Create user role
                    activate t_user_role
                        note right of t_user_role
                            INSERT INTO author.t_user_role (
                                created_by,
                                created_at,
                                row_status,
                                user_id,
                                role_id
                            )
                            VALUES (
                                &#39;<sequence.createdBy>',
                                &#39;<sequence.now>',
                                &#39;<sequence.rowStatus>',
                                &#39;<sequence.userId>',
                                &#39;<sequence.roleId>'
                            )
                            RETURNING id as user_role_id
                        end note
                        t_user_role -> infra: Return inserted user_role_id
                    deactivate t_user_role
                    infra -> app: Return inserted user_role_id
                    app -> app: Require exactly one inserted user_role_id; missing/malformed result is internal failure; action = INSERT
                else id is specified (UPDATE, DELETE or ARCHIVE)
                    app -> infra: UPDATE - Update, archive or delete user role
                    infra -> t_user_role: UPDATE - Update, archive or delete user role
                    activate t_user_role
                        note right of t_user_role
                            UPDATE author.t_user_role
                            SET
                                updated_by = '<sequence.updatedBy>',
                                updated_at = '<sequence.now>',
                                row_status = '<sequence.rowStatus>'
                            WHERE id = '<sequence.id>'
                            AND row_status <> 'DELETED'
                            RETURNING id as user_role_id
                        end note
                        t_user_role -> infra: Return guarded returned user_role_id or no row
                    deactivate t_user_role
                    infra -> app: Return guarded returned user_role_id or no row
                    alt Guarded UPDATE returned zero rows
                        break Reject this request
                            app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                            app -> api: HTTP 404 E10004 User role not found.
                            api -> page: Show failure; no successful user role action
                            page -> user: Display failure; keep unsaved input
                        end break
                    else Check passed
                    end
                    app -> app: Require exactly one returned user_role_id equal to this input id; mismatch is internal failure
                    app -> app: action = DELETE for DELETED, ARCHIVE for ARCHIVED, otherwise UPDATE
                end
                app -> infra: QUERY - Count the platform administrators after the write
                infra -> t_user_role: QUERY - Count the platform administrators after the write
                activate t_user_role
                    note right of t_user_role
                        SELECT
                            COUNT(ur.id) as administrators
                        FROM author.t_user_role ur
                        INNER JOIN author.m_role r
                            ON r.id = ur.role_id
                                AND r.name = 'PLATFORM_ADMIN'
                                AND r.row_status = 'ACTIVE'
                        INNER JOIN authen.m_user u
                            ON u.id = ur.user_id
                                AND u.row_status = 'ACTIVE'
                        WHERE ur.row_status = 'ACTIVE' -- the request is rolled back (409) when the count is 0
                    end note
                    t_user_role -> infra: Return the number of ACTIVE PLATFORM_ADMIN assignments whose user is ACTIVE
                deactivate t_user_role
                infra -> app: Return the number of ACTIVE PLATFORM_ADMIN assignments whose user is ACTIVE
                alt No ACTIVE administrator is left after the write
                    break Reject this request
                        app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                        app -> api: HTTP 409 E10006 The platform must keep at least one administrator.
                        api -> page: Show failure; no successful user role action
                        page -> user: Display failure; keep unsaved input
                    end break
                else Check passed
                end
                app -> app: Map data.userRoleId from RETURNING before COMMIT; delete maps no body
                app -> infra: COMMIT
                infra -> app: Return committed assignment
                alt Insert
                    note over app, infra
                        Detailed revision remains in-review; no schema/backend implementation.
                        Only a platform administrator from the verified JWT roles claim can assign or take away a role; require
                        exact case-sensitive role name PLATFORM_ADMIN. A valid non-admin claim returns 403 E10009 after the
                        existence checks and before the duplicate check, including when it gives the role `PLATFORM_ADMIN` to
                        another user. No live caller-assignment or request-flag fallback. Approved by the product owner
                        (Q2/Q4/Q10/Q13); this supersedes the earlier live-grant guard.
                        Taking the role away (`rowStatus` DELETED, ARCHIVED, INACTIVE or LOCKED) works whatever the status of the
                        user and of the role is, so that a role cannot stay on a locked or closed account and come back when the
                        account is opened again. The target user row must exist for every request: a missing target user is 404
                        (E10005) `User not found.`, also when the request takes the role away. The last administrator rule below
                        still applies in full. `userId` and `roleId` are required in every request and cannot be changed by an
                        update: a different value from the row of `id` is 400 (E10001). Approved by the product owner on 2026-11-08
                        (target-row locks and the missing-target-user answer).
                        A row that is INACTIVE, LOCKED or ARCHIVED still holds the place and gives no right, an update with
                        `rowStatus` ACTIVE opens it again. After a delete the role can be assigned again, which creates a new row.
                        DELETED is final: a DELETED row never reopens and its `id` counts as not found (404, E10004). `rowStatus`
                        DELETED is rejected with 400 (E10001) when the request inserts a row.
                        **The platform keeps at least one administrator.** After the whole request is applied there must be at least
                        one ACTIVE `t_user_role` row of the ACTIVE role `PLATFORM_ADMIN` whose user is ACTIVE, otherwise 409
                        (E10006) and the request is rolled back. This covers deleting, archiving, locking or deactivating the last
                        assignment, including when an administrator takes the role away from themselves. An administrator cannot
                        skip this rule. The rule is checked on the state after the write.
                        Authorize only exact `PLATFORM_ADMIN` in verified JWT roles after current credentials and existence checks.
                        [] or any other valid role name gives 403 E10009 You do not have permission to assign roles.; do not query
                        live caller role grants. The `PLATFORM_ADMIN` name is read from the locked role row and from the
                        administrator count only to protect the last-administrator invariant, never to authorize the caller.
                        Bind all values. A locked assignment is the single source for the stored user, role and status; an update
                        that sets ACTIVE on a row that is not ACTIVE counts as giving the role. Duplicate exclusion is null-safe:
                        omitted insert id binds typed SQL NULL. INSERT explicitly sets created_at and must return exactly one
                        user_role_id UUID; missing/malformed result is generic 500. UPDATE guards id and non-DELETED status; zero
                        returned rows is 404 E10004 with rollback. Preserve created_by/created_at on UPDATE. Map exactly
                        data.userRoleId from RETURNING before COMMIT.
                    end note
                    app -> api: HTTP 201 S10000 Insert User Role Success
                    api -> page: Return the user role
                    page -> user: Display the outcome
                else rowStatus = DELETED (delete)
                    app -> api: HTTP 204 No Content; no response body
                    api -> page: No content
                    page -> user: Display the outcome
                else rowStatus = ARCHIVED (archive)
                    app -> api: HTTP 200 S10000 Archive User Role Success
                    api -> page: Return the user role
                    page -> user: Display the outcome
                else Update
                    app -> api: HTTP 200 S10000 Update User Role Success
                    api -> page: Return the user role
                    page -> user: Display the outcome
                end
            else SQLSTATE 23505 from uq_t_user_role_user_id_role_id (concurrent duplicate)
                app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                app -> api: HTTP 409 E10003 The user already has this role.
                api -> page: Conflict
                page -> user: Display the outcome
            else Timeout before COMMIT
                app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                app -> api: HTTP 408 E90001
                api -> page: Request timeout
                page -> user: Display the outcome
            else Unexpected SQL/result/mapping failure before COMMIT
                app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                app -> api: HTTP 500 Internal Server Error; omit bizCode
                api -> page: Internal server error
                page -> user: Display the outcome
            end
            deactivate infra
        deactivate app
    deactivate api
deactivate page
@enduml
